A||||6||MCordray||Flickering Lights...||||13||
Z||000000||MCordray||12-01-1999||06:54 PM||||Lately, I've noticed that my headlights and interior dome lights flicker somewhat rapidly when I'm idling in drive or just in park. Any ideas on what this could be? I've recently replaced the alternator, battery, plugs, and wires. Could this have anything to do with the distributor and or coil?  ||||reg||13
Z||000001||Cooter||12-01-1999||08:12 PM||||A bad regulator in the alternator will do this and not make the warning light come on. Pull the Alternator and have it checked soon because that unstable voltage cant be good for old electronics.||||reg||1
Z||000002||kornholio||12-01-1999||08:26 PM||||Hey Cooter,<BR>Instead of pulling out the alternator to get it tested, couldn't you just test the voltage with a voltmeter at the battery when the car is running?  Will the battery still be charging at 14v when the regulator's bad?||||reg||5
Z||000003||Cooter||12-01-1999||11:21 PM||||That depends on the reaction timing of the voltmeter. Most digital volt meters will "average" the input reading to make it a stable, more readable display. Also, the battery itself will buffer the voltage readings and may mask the quick changes in voltage that MCordray is describing. Another thought is the rectifier bridge or diode trio may be bad allowing AC voltage to go through the system. I hate pulling alternators, but I still think that I would do it because my old Z-28 fried a rebuilt alternator in about a month of driving. It was doing the same thing as MCordray's and the only way I noticed it was the flickering headlights.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MCordray||12-02-1999||06:49 PM||||Cooter, kornholio... Thanks for the responses. I had a feeling it was the alternator, but I was REALLY hoping it wasn't. I'm not looking forward to pulling the alternator out AGAIN.||||reg||1
Z||000005||burdell1||12-02-1999||07:55 PM||||Did you have problems with your car radio screeching when the lights were flickering? I am having a similar problem with my '85 GT.||||reg||1
Z||000006||MCordray||12-04-1999||10:38 AM||||The radio was fine. I only notice it in the lighting system. Since posting this topic, I had the alternator checked out by Autozone. My voltage regulator check out fine. But, I can see my voltage dash needle move slightly back and forth. The parts guy suggested a short in the system. Anybody have any ideas?!? ||||reg||1
